00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:05.680
Nicole: User Access control or UAC
is a mandatory access control feature

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:09.799
which was introduced by Microsoft
to improve the security of Microsoft

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:14.760
Windows by limiting user privileges
until authorised by the administrator.

00:00:15.349 --> 00:00:19.320
This was done to prevent malware from
compromising the operating system.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:25.070
User access control generally manages
user accounts particularly those with

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:29.920
special access privileges to protect
against misuse and unauthorised access.

00:00:30.799 --> 00:00:34.449
To help keep a system secure, accounts
should only be assigned to authorised

00:00:35.819 --> 00:00:40.070
individuals and should limit access to the
minimum level needed by the individual.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:45.269
Failure to implement an effective
user access control management policy,

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:50.519
may expose an organisations system
to cyber attack as it makes it easier

00:00:50.519 --> 00:00:54.940
for hackers to take advantage of
uncontrolled administrative privileges.

00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:59.680
One of the techniques used to attack
a system involves the elevation

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:03.450
of privileges by guessing and
cracking administrator passwords

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:05.940
to gain access to target machines.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:11.359
So, let’s look at how user access
controls be managed effectively?

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:16.610
• By having a user account management
system and privilege management process.

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:21.670
• Not using network and systems
administrator accounts for other

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:23.439
non-administrator activities.

00:01:24.059 --> 00:01:26.940
• Restricting privileges to
authorised individuals.

00:01:27.799 --> 00:01:32.190
• Set up device-based authentication
allowing only certain devices

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:33.400
to access the network.

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:36.420
• Keeping records of user access permissions

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:41.450
• Implementing a strong password and
unique username policy ensuring that

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:43.269
passwords are changed regularly.

00:01:44.049 --> 00:01:47.539
• Restricting the ability to
install third party software

00:01:48.549 --> 00:01:52.690
The overall goal of User Access
Control is to protect the system

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:56.500
and maintain the cyber security
of an organisation or company.

00:01:57.150 --> 00:02:00.580
It is also used in households
where parents can restrict internet

00:02:00.679 --> 00:02:04.429
access to children in the household
but often for different reasons.

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:09.410
It may annoy users that they may not
have full access, but by limiting

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:13.570
access to the absolute minimum needed
to fulfil their role, there is less

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:17.940
chance of cyber attacks happening
therefore making the system more secure.

